OpenCode server
===============
The opencode2 package includes an optional runit service named opencode.
It is not enabled automatically. To enable it:

    ln -s /etc/sv/opencode /var/service/

Configure /etc/sv/opencode/conf, then run `sv restart opencode` after changes.
The default endpoint is http://127.0.0.1:4096. Set a strong
OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD before listening on a non-loopback address.

The service runs as _opencode, with HOME=/var/lib/opencode. Its credentials,
configuration and sessions are separate from your interactive user's data.
Configure providers for this account and grant it access only to the projects
it needs. OPENCODE_DIRECTORY selects its working directory.

OpenCode desktop
================
Install opencode2-desktop and launch OpenCode from your application menu or
run `opencode-desktop`. The desktop uses the CLI from opencode2; the runit
service is not required for desktop use.
